@startuml
title Prediction Cards System Architecture
left to right direction
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam maxMessageSize 220

rectangle "User Frontend (React)" as FE {
  component "Prediction UI" as UI
  component "Prediction API\n(Provider/Context)" as API
  component "Aeternity Wallet Client\n+ SDK" as WALLET
}

package "Aeternity Blockchain" as CHAIN {
  component "PredictionCards\nSmart Contract" as CONTRACT
  component "AENS Name Service" as AENS
  component "Oracle Registry\n& Oracle Queries" as OREG
}

node "Backend Services" as SRV {
  component "Prediction-Processing Service" as PPS
  component "Oracle Service (Quarkus)" as ORACLE
}

cloud "Prediction Media Storage\n(IPFS-compatible)" as MEDIA
cloud "External Price Provider" as PRICE

frame "Local Contract Integration-Test Stack" as TEST {
  component "AE Node" as NODE
  component "Compiler Service" as COMP
  component "Index Service" as IDX
  component "Debug Endpoint" as DBG
  component "Test Proxy\n(CORS Enabled)" as PROXY
}

' Frontend interactions
UI --> API : User operations
API --> WALLET : Wallet connection/sign & contract calls
API ..> AENS : Resolve contract by AENS name
WALLET --> CONTRACT : Create/View predictions;\nFund/Rent/Withdraw; Claim rewards
API --> MEDIA : Load outcome NFT media

' Prediction-processing service workflow
PPS ..> AENS : Resolve contract
PPS --> CONTRACT : 5. Initiate oracle query\n7. Drive on-chain result processing

' On-chain oracle objects
CONTRACT --> OREG : Create pending\noracle query objects

' Oracle service responsibilities
ORACLE ..> AENS : Resolve contract
ORACLE --> PRICE : Obtain external price data
ORACLE --> OREG : 6. Submit oracle response\n(result: higher | lower_or_equal)
ORACLE --> OREG : Check/Register/Extend\noracle validity

' Local integration-test flows (CORS/proxy)
FE --> PROXY : Local browser requests\nGET/POST/OPTIONS; headers:\nContent-Type, Cache-Control,\nContent-Range, Range
PROXY --> NODE
PROXY --> COMP
PROXY --> IDX
PROXY --> DBG

' Notes on responsibilities and constraints
note right of ORACLE
Scheduled periodic processing:\n- Check pending oracle queries\n- Maintain oracle registration/validity\n- Query price provider and submit responses
end note

note right of PPS
Scheduled handling of closed predictions:\n- Discover closed predictions\n- Initiate oracle queries\n- Complete on-chain result processing
end note

note right of API
Contract interaction rules:\n- Convert local times to millisecond timestamps (DR-009)\n- Use connected wallet dependency (FR-007)\n- Provide operations via provider/context (FR-005)
end note

note right of OREG
Oracle result enumeration:\n- higher\n- lower_or_equal
end note

note bottom of CHAIN
On-chain state holds predictions, outcomes, and\nreward-claiming availability after result processing.
end note

@enduml